From e70bc7513fab8aa926189f24c3f0d0b100740b6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:19:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: a0-relative constants in Xenos pixel shaders
 too

Pixel shaders can read constants at a0 as well. Two things kept them
from it:

- An export's ALLOC loses a0 (found by xsdk, github.com/xenosworks/xsdk,
  docs/HARDWARE.md, "a0 doesn't survive an alloc"). The scheduler no
  longer issues an export between a MOVA and its relative read, and
  cp_export no longer turns a relative read into an export.
- fd2's constant split, vertex constants from 0x20 and pixel constants
  from 0x120 (size 0xe0): relative reads in a pixel shader read nothing
  at any index with it. Use the split libxenon and xsdk use, vertex
  constants from 0 and pixel constants from 0x100, 256 each (the size
  field is size - 1). VS_CONST_BASE/PS_CONST_BASE move to fd2_emit.h and
  the clear-color constant writes use PS_CONST_BASE.

indirect_const_addr is now set for both stages on Xenos. piglit
glsl-uniform-interstage-limits subdivide 5 (and with statechanges)
pass; they crashed out of registers on the if/else tree. dEQP
17063/17075, no regressions; performance unchanged.

